{"code": 200, "results": [{"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2084638878548304046", "id": "2084638878548304046", "text": "I've been working on an orchestration harness for a squad of agents.  I want to have a squad leader agent that supervises a bevy of workers.  The workers are analysts, reviewers, gherkin authors, QA authors, implementers, cleaners, code reviewers, hardeners, QA testers, architects, and senior implementers.  \n\nThere is a fixed workflow from themes to stories to gherkin and QA, to code, unit tests, and acceptance tests, to cleaned code, to hardened code, to QA'd code, to architecture.\n\nThis fixed workflow can be described by a static FSM.  So I had my agents build it.  Then I had my agents build a simulator of my  squad and drive the simulator through the FSM.  Then I had them jitter the simulator, simulating delays and failures.  I had them run monte-carlo testing for many runs.  \n\nThe agents never would have thought of that kind of testing regime.  They never would have build the simulator on their own and engaged in monte-carlo testing.\n\nDon't tell me software engineering is dead.", "raw_text": {"text": "I've been working on an orchestration harness for a squad of agents.  I want to have a squad leader agent that supervises a bevy of workers.  The workers are analysts, reviewers, gherkin authors, QA authors, implementers, cleaners, code reviewers, hardeners, QA testers, architects, and senior implementers.  \n\nThere is a fixed workflow from themes to stories to gherkin and QA, to code, unit tests, and acceptance tests, to cleaned code, to hardened code, to QA'd code, to architecture.\n\nThis fixed workflow can be described by a static FSM.  So I had my agents build it.  Then I had my agents build a simulator of my  squad and drive the simulator through the FSM.  Then I had them jitter the simulator, simulating delays and failures.  I had them run monte-carlo testing for many runs.  \n\nThe agents never would have thought of that kind of testing regime.  They never would have build the simulator on their own and engaged in monte-carlo testing.\n\nDon't tell me software engineering is dead.", "display_text_range": [0, 996], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 149, "reposts": 148, "likes": 2058, "bookmarks": 1689, "quotes": 23, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Tue Aug 04 13:53:34 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1785851614, "views": 156845, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2084624628031361384", "id": "2084624628031361384", "text": "Special Message from the Office of Approved Opinions Regarding the Ceuta... https://youtu.be/wWorpZhbhYQ?si=ZXmYuOyQnD1Blg1M via @YouTube", "raw_text": {"text": "Special Message from the Office of Approved Opinions Regarding the Ceuta... https://t.co/BsqnSJ1iuR via @YouTube", "display_text_range": [0, 112], "facets": [{"type": "url", "indices": [76, 99], "original": "https://t.co/BsqnSJ1iuR", "replacement": "https://youtu.be/wWorpZhbhYQ?si=ZXmYuOyQnD1Blg1M", "display": "youtu.be/wWorpZhbhYQ?si\u2026"}, {"type": "mention", 